Package: autoSpectra
Title: Soil Spectral Modeling, Visualization and Prediction
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Hugo",
    family = "Rodrigues",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "rodrigues.machado.hugo@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8070-8126"))
Description: Predicts soil physical and chemical properties from diffuse
    reflectance spectra (visible-near-infrared, 400-2500 nm, and
    mid-infrared, 600-4000 cm-1) with models trained on the Open Soil
    Spectral Library (OSSL v1.2). Two model families are provided: a 'Cubist'
    model on 120 principal components that replicates the OSSL methodology
    of Safanelli et al. (2025) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0296545>, and the
    same pipeline with 'Cubist' replaced by an ensemble of supervised
    variational autoencoders from the 'soilVAE' package. Instruments that
    cover only part of the spectral range are handled by models trained on
    the matching instrument window. Predictions come with conformal
    prediction intervals and applicability-domain checks. Pre-trained models
    are downloaded on request from Zenodo; functions to train models,
    including for a user's own instrument, and a 'shiny' interface are
    included.
